{"title":"1961 AHSME Problems/Problem 25","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is isosceles with base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> are respectively in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e3a4ec0df571e719bd3f1d7e00bf71fc55ba2b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/1/fb11700c1232e927eeefa96614e41807e315a32a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=AP=PQ=QB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"185\" height=\"16\" />. \nThe number of degrees in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/1/2918f7d23f9ee8c04baabad86100d68023ec03f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/8/a788a0f0937e934f4a97b81ce0b6db0a7f8f5a65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 25\\frac{5}{7}\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 26\\frac{1}{3}\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 30\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 40\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{Not determined by the information given}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"703\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:1961_AHSME_Problem_25.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/48/1961_AHSME_Problem_25.png/300px-1961_AHSME_Problem_25.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"288\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/48/1961_AHSME_Problem_25.png/450px-1961_AHSME_Problem_25.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/48/1961_AHSME_Problem_25.png/600px-1961_AHSME_Problem_25.png 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> be the measure of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/1/2918f7d23f9ee8c04baabad86100d68023ec03f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/0/35089e8ea9a9a45425fe62d58d560fe8c3568c31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BQP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"17\" /> is an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Isosceles_triangle\" title=\"Isosceles triangle\">isosceles triangle</a>, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/7/bd7d438bb7e1db4e9268dda1319423a69b3e7684.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BPQ = b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"88\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/e/2aeff7d59b60b54a1a1e5526d890f5d08c441644.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BQP = 180 - 2b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"147\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is a line, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/9/cf9725859ba045c4316aa981742bf0a125cc7fce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AQP = 2b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"96\" height=\"16\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/c/59ccfb86baf6bd54a12b75424f360397a0273c67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle QPA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"17\" /> is isosceles as well, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab6fcbd6f59bec468cc0ae5474f3592ee656ade.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle QAP = 2b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"96\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/b/78bf147d499a1a0d62293397a651845eaa175ca5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle QPA = 180 - 4b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"146\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is a line, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/0/9e068655dce13dad6ae0defb3fec16d05162457e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle APC = 3b$\" width=\"96\" height=\"13\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/5/14589098013cf51bd13b7d32a5476db3ee28f0cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle APC$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is isosceles as well, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/6/df603a38755394eec74fa2378da4a74129741b60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACB = 3b$\" width=\"96\" height=\"13\" />.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is also isosceles, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a1d6f92728da4899bc591b5a696fabe67f3f40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC = 3b$\" width=\"96\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/c/ddcafe2df15bf11271e2e770b904ca7f782e12ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PAC = b$\" width=\"87\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>The angles in a triangle add up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/b/5cb1b41850ab676e4d1cf15c69b1609af4befbc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> degrees, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/f/4dfab043fad6cb65e3a29585885cc591e83b8bc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3b + 3b + b = 180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"137\" height=\"14\" />.  Solving the equation yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/d/bed9babfbea95b124b956ebd954d904ee8112002.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = \\frac{180}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"61\" height=\"37\" />.  Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/0/1103311b28e0d583804af643f2b37ac81a13132b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle B = 25\\frac{5}{7}^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"89\" height=\"38\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/e/35e8ea2d16518197b5113002b8c0c7da6c311a3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"41\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME\" title=\"1961 AHSME\">1961 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1961 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1961 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1961\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1961 AHSME Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"1961 AHSME Problems/Problem 26\">Problem 26</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1961 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1961 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1961 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1961 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" 